  "parentCard": {
    "title": "Be the shop's first customer",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "cut-draw",
    "steps": [
      "Before the stand opens, a grown-up puts three coins in your purse, and your older sibling works out which things on their table cost three coins today, so that whatever you choose, your coins are exactly enough.",
      "At the table, choose one thing yourself. Nobody chooses for you, and taking a long time to choose is allowed.",
      "Count the coins into your older sibling's hand one at a time and say the numbers out loud: one, two, three. They hold their hand still and wait however long it takes, and if you lose your place you start again.",
      "Take your thing somewhere quiet with paper and crayons and draw what you bought, with the three coins drawn beside it.",
      "Cut your drawing out and give it to your older sibling to keep at their shop. A grown-up holds the scissors if the cutting is tricky, and you do the choosing and the peeling off."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Do they count each coin as it leaves their hand, or tip all three in and count afterwards?",
      "Can they say how many coins they gave once the coins are inside a hand they cannot see into?",
      "What do they draw first, the thing they bought or the coins they paid with?"
    ]
  }
